{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently underestimates the magnitude of upward trends, failing to capture the rapid price escalation (e.g., 77 to 98) seen in true outcomes.",
    "Eliminate excessive mean reversion: The model assumes prices will stabilize near recent lows (77-80) after dips, whereas the market exhibits strong momentum and fails to revert to the mean, instead breaking previous highs.",
    "Adjust for lag in trend detection: Forecasts react too slowly to positive sentiment spikes (0.20), often predicting flat or declining paths while the actual market is in a sustained bull run.",
    "Remove artificial ceiling effects: The model imposes a soft cap around 88-90, ignoring the structural breakout potential that pushes prices to 95-100 during periods of positive sentiment.",
    "Incorporate momentum scaling: When sentiment history shows consecutive positive signals or a history of rising prices, increase the forecast slope significantly rather than flattening it."
  ]
}
